<template>
    <children>
        <li id="34.lp5"/>
        <li id="33.lp5"/>
        <li id="32.lp5"/>
    </children>
    <heading>Model</heading>
    <keywords>
        <li>model</li>
        <li>project</li>
        <li>directory handle</li>
        <li>IndexedDB</li>
    </keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p><code>window.LP5.model</code> owns the current directory handle privately; it exposes no getter for that handle. Its interface is <code>await model.selectProject(handle)</code>, which stores the supplied handle in IndexedDB and then installs it as the current selection. It returns no handle.</p>
        <p>Selection delegates persistence to <code>util.indexedDB.storeDirectoryHandle(handle)</code>. Previously selected directories remain available in the persistent set. If storage fails, the Promise rejects and the current in-memory selection is preserved.</p>
        <p>The selected handle is used by <code>loadProject()</code>, described in the child articles. Restoring saved selections and checking permissions remain later work. The model does not open the picker or perform UI work.</p>
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 700 570" role="img"
             aria-labelledby="modelStructureTitle modelStructureDescription"
             style="display:block; width:min(100%, 700px); height:auto; margin:1rem auto; font:17px sans-serif">
            <title id="modelStructureTitle">Loaded project data structures</title>
            <desc id="modelStructureDescription">The root filename selects an article in a filename map. Each article record owns a detached XML document and a parent filename. Ordered child links in XML define document traversal. Bundle and referrer maps point to these same article records.</desc>
            <defs>
                <marker id="modelStructureArrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5"
                        markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                    <path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10Z" fill="#526174"/>
                </marker>
            </defs>
            <rect x="1" y="1" width="698" height="568" rx="8" fill="#fff" stroke="#a1adba"/>
            <g fill="#17283a">
                <text x="24" y="34" font-weight="bold">Loaded model — example project</text>
                <text x="24" y="65">rootFilename = "demo.lp5"</text>
            </g>
            <path d="M134 75V105" fill="none" stroke="#526174" stroke-width="2"
                  marker-end="url(#modelStructureArrow)"/>

            <rect x="18" y="112" width="238" height="197" rx="6" fill="#edf2f7" stroke="#7890aa"/>
            <g fill="#17283a">
                <text x="34" y="140" font-weight="bold">articles: Map</text>
                <text x="34" y="168">filename → article record</text>
                <text x="34" y="203">"demo.lp5" → root</text>
                <text x="34" y="239">"1.lp5" →</text>
                <text x="34" y="275">"2.lp5" → another record</text>
            </g>
            <path d="M131 233H283" fill="none" stroke="#526174" stroke-width="2"
                  marker-end="url(#modelStructureArrow)"/>

            <rect x="291" y="112" width="391" height="197" rx="6" fill="#e8f2eb" stroke="#7d9c84"/>
            <g fill="#203b29">
                <text x="307" y="140" font-weight="bold">Article record for "1.lp5"</text>
                <text x="307" y="171">filename: "1.lp5"</text>
                <text x="307" y="202">parentFilename: "demo.lp5"</text>
                <text x="307" y="233">document: detached XMLDocument</text>
                <text x="307" y="264">Owns &lt;template&gt;, sections, code,</text>
                <text x="307" y="289">and ordered &lt;children&gt; links.</text>
            </g>

            <rect x="18" y="329" width="664" height="86" rx="6" fill="#f7f4e8" stroke="#b5a36e"/>
            <g fill="#342d1c">
                <text x="34" y="354" font-weight="bold">Tree order comes from the XML child links</text>
                <text x="34" y="387">demo.lp5</text>
                <text x="250" y="387">1.lp5</text>
                <text x="451" y="387">2.lp5</text>
            </g>
            <g fill="none" stroke="#526174" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#modelStructureArrow)">
                <path d="M142 381H234"/>
                <path d="M314 381H435"/>
            </g>

            <rect x="18" y="435" width="321" height="89" rx="6" fill="#dce8f5" stroke="#7890aa"/>
            <rect x="359" y="435" width="323" height="89" rx="6" fill="#dce8f5" stroke="#7890aa"/>
            <g fill="#17283a">
                <text x="34" y="462" font-weight="bold">bundles: Map</text>
                <text x="34" y="489">"Shared" → [1.lp5, 2.lp5]</text>
                <text x="34" y="513">Definitions in document order</text>
                <text x="375" y="462" font-weight="bold">referrers: Map</text>
                <text x="375" y="489">"Shared" → {demo.lp5}</text>
                <text x="375" y="513">Articles referencing the bundle</text>
                <text x="350" y="552" text-anchor="middle">Both indexes reference the same records; they do not copy XML.</text>
            </g>
        </svg>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code">
        <name>JavaScript units</name>
        <code><![CDATA[let model = (() => {
    let directoryHandle = null;
    let articles = new Map();
    let rootFilename = null;
    let bundles = new Map();
    let referrers = new Map();

    async function selectProject(handle) {
        await util.indexedDB.storeDirectoryHandle(handle);
        directoryHandle = handle;
    }

    ]]><lp5- ref="Model article XML"/><lp5- ref="Model bundle indexes"/><lp5- ref="Model project loading"/><![CDATA[

    return {
        selectProject,
        loadProject,
        get rootFilename() { return rootFilename; },
        getArticle,
        docOrder,
        getBundle,
        getReferrers
    };
})();
]]></code>
    </section>
</template>
